From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] charset: the single-byte codecs as the Encoding Standard's
 indexes

The WHATWG Encoding Standard's indexes, which browsers decode with, give
the ISO-8859 encodings' bytes 0x80-0x9F the C1 controls U+0080-U+009F,
the Windows code pages' unassigned bytes in 0x80-0x9F theirs too, and
windows-1255's 0xCA U+05BA (HEBREW POINT HOLAM HASER FOR VAV). The 8859
codec treated 0x80-0x9F as invalid and the ext8 tables had U+FFFF there,
so such a byte became U+FFFD: in a page's text, and in a link's or form's
query, which a browser sends as the byte and EWeb sent as &#65533;. Now
the 8859 codec decodes and encodes 0x80-0x9F as themselves and the ext8
tables have the indexes' code points; the bytes the indexes leave out
stay U+FFFF.
---
 src/charset/codecs/codec_8859.c  | 13 ++++---
 src/charset/codecs/ext8_tables.h | 64 +++++++++++++++++---------------
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/charset/codecs/codec_8859.c b/src/charset/codecs/codec_8859.c
index 8027d3b0..fd36b3a7 100644
--- a/src/charset/codecs/codec_8859.c
+++ b/src/charset/codecs/codec_8859.c
@@ -521,8 +521,9 @@ parserutils_error charset_8859_from_ucs4(charset_8859_codec *c,
 	if (*len < 1)
 		return PARSERUTILS_NOMEM;
 
-	if (ucs4 < 0x80) {
-		/* ASCII */
+	if (ucs4 < 0xA0) {
+		/* ASCII, and (EWeb) the C1 controls as the WHATWG Encoding
+		 * Standard's indexes have them */
 		out = ucs4;
 	} else {
 		uint32_t i;
@@ -569,15 +570,15 @@ parserutils_error charset_8859_to_ucs4(charset_8859_codec *c,
 	if (len < 1)
 		return PARSERUTILS_NEEDDATA;
 
-	if (*s < 0x80) {
+	if (*s < 0xA0) {
+		/* ASCII, and (EWeb) 0x80-0x9F the C1 controls, as the WHATWG
+		 * Encoding Standard's indexes have them */
 		out = *s;
-	} else if (*s >= 0xA0) {
+	} else {
 		if (c->table[*s - 0xA0] == 0xFFFF)
 			return PARSERUTILS_INVALID;
 
 		out = c->table[*s - 0xA0];
-	} else {
-		return PARSERUTILS_INVALID;
 	}
 
 	*ucs4 = out;
